00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,190
Most inference optimizers ask one question: which configuration is fastest?

2
00:00:04,190 --> 00:00:11,220
AArchTune asks a harder one: which configuration is faster, correct, reproducible, and safe to deploy on native Arm64?

3
00:00:11,220 --> 00:00:18,420
It tunes GGUF inference through llama.cpp, but it refuses to turn a fast, incorrect response into a recommendation.

